  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\axiom.of.pairing]\nAxiom:\ngiven: X, Y is \\set\nthen:\n. exists: U is \\set\n  suchThat:\n  . forAll: Z is \\set\n    then: (Z \"in\"? U) \\.iff./ ((.Z = X.) \\.or./ (.Z = Y.))\nDocumented:\n. called: \"Axiom of Pairing\"\n. description: \"For any two sets $X$ and $Y$ there is a set $U$ whose members\n                are exactly $X$ and $Y$. Applying it with $X = Y$ produces the\n                set whose only member is $X$.\"\nId: \"3219aca1-fba1-42a6-9a1f-209aa430c677\"",
